{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536178-could-killing-maeljin-incarna-actually-reduce-humanity-s-population","id":1536178,"title":"Could killing Maeljin Incarna actually reduce humanity's population?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-23T18:21:26-07:00","id":1536178,"title":"Could killing Maeljin Incarna actually reduce humanity's population?","content":"So, if you kill a Maeljin Incarna, it's presence on Earth will be reduced. But how will a human brain and even body respond to that? Say you have an antivaxer incel who is a Qanoner, who's entire reality and identity is formed around lies, fear, paranoia, a seething hatred and a desire to &quot;destroy&quot; the other painfully and humiliatingly, and a steadfast refusal to change beliefs despite evidence. Then, miraculously, the different Maeljin Incarna that embodies these psychological traits suddenly are destroyed along with their duchies. If the traits that make up the very core of who and what these people are suddenly vanish, or are even just severely diminished from the world, even for a few days, could it cause brain injury, coma, or even possible brain death? Especially in the elderly?<br /> <br /> What would be the logical fates of those who are already pretty well swallowed by the Wyrm?<br /> <br /> Basically, would slaying aspects of the Wyrm actually create a smaller Apocalypse, albeit one that humanity and the Earth could survive from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 05-23-2024, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T18:42:35-07:00","id":1536179,"title":"","content":"To my understanding Maeljin Incarna are more like representatives of that particular concept, but they don't embody it. We know that Malejin Incarna have been killed and replaced before (some of them with quite a bit of frequency). For example Lady Aife was one an inquisitor in the Spanish Inquisition, but it's not like the concept of Desire didn't exist before he took her position as a Maeljin Incarna. So if you killed a Maeljin Incarna, there would be one fewer Wyrm minions out there looking to spread corruption and insanity and over time other Wyrm minions would begin fighting and warring for the now vacant position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T19:30:36-07:00","id":1536182,"title":"","content":"The Book of the Wyrm was explicit about how killing one of the Maeljin, or even just their duchy, reduced the presence of what it embodied on Earth. That humans would find it strange but natural how the world had improved but the Fera would understand what had happened. And also that, at the very least, it might take centuries for it to be recreated by the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T19:54:52-07:00","id":1536183,"title":"","content":"Your idea of what it means for these things to be a deep and abiding part of a person's character sounds deeply literal, never mind oddly physiological. The description you've given from The Book of the Wyrm sounds a lot more like a reduced presence of those concepts in the world amounting to a person of that type losing a lot of their driving force and dedication than something like having their physical brain matter excised. It might be psychologically traumatic, but I can't see it being so biological.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T20:06:59-07:00","id":1536184,"title":"","content":"If it is all they think about all day, if they make up the core of who they are, to the point there isn\u2019t much else inside to take its place if those concepts are strongly reduced, it seems like this might cause psychological or even physiological damage to the individuals affected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T22:48:15-07:00","id":1536190,"title":"","content":"Far more likely, they would be cowed and concentrate on to the &quot;hawking junk health supplements&quot; part of their grift before slowly losing relevance and emerging from their dank basement dungeon to get a job, walk around in a daze and in awe at the world, or any number of other events. To actually be incapacitated or suffer injury would suggest that they had a very direct connection to the Maeljin in question, like being ridden or possessed by one of its more direct minions, and that said minion died in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T08:07:35-07:00","id":1536205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536178-could-killing-maeljin-incarna-actually-reduce-humanity-s-population?p=1536184#post1536184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is all they think about all day, if they make up the core of who they are, to the point there isn\u2019t much else inside to take its place if those concepts are strongly reduced, it seems like this might cause psychological or even physiological damage to the individuals affected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to accommodate that this increasingly caricatured picture at least sounds like a plausible inhabitant of the World of Darkness, but I'll say again that your own description of the relevant text in another book makes it sound more like a subtle withdrawal than a violent wrenching. An individual might experience a form of trauma in the form of finding themselves confronted with an existential crisis of losing investment in something that they had become severely dedicated to, but at the baseline it just sounds like an effect that would make a person become incredibly boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T10:55:46-07:00","id":1536215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536178-could-killing-maeljin-incarna-actually-reduce-humanity-s-population?p=1536205#post1536205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to accommodate that this increasingly caricatured picture at least sounds like a plausible inhabitant of the World of Darkness, but I'll say again that your own description of the relevant text in another book makes it sound more like a subtle withdrawal than a violent wrenching. An individual might experience a form of trauma in the form of finding themselves confronted with an existential crisis of losing investment in something that they had become severely dedicated to, but at the baseline it just sounds like an effect that would make a person become incredibly boring.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a good point. After reviewing the exact text, it is supposed to be a natural seeming transition. I was hoping for something dramatic and world shattering, but honestly a fade in to a better world also works.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T15:05:31-07:00","id":1536219,"title":"","content":"If you want them to go with a Bang, there are other options.<br /> <br /> Once such an entity dies, you could have their minions going through a rampage as they try to desperately impose the lost level of (whatever they represent). Maybe most withdraw to lick their likely wounds, but some go on a possession spree or something.<br /> <br /> But in the end, history says it already happened and they go without much notice from the human world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T02:08:03-07:00","id":1536237,"title":"","content":"Eh I feel like if you destroy those Maeljin Incarna, it would be more like in Persona 5 when you steal the treasure of the persons unnatural desire. So suddenly all those feelings of those that feel them extreme are gone and instead it is left what else they have that made them human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T14:45:51-07:00","id":1536318,"title":"","content":"I feel the key here is that the Maeljin are not the causes of Evil. They are walking talking feedback loops of pettyness, abuse and horror. They feed of humans being horrible to each other, and they encourage people to be horrible in turn. This empowers them to do more crap in the world, whisper to susceptible people and create fomori and other direct or indirect servants.<br /> <br /> If you kill one of them, you do not remove the concepts of suffering from the world or magically stop humans from being mean assholes. You just stop that urge being proactive and lower its impact on the world. That doesn't mean you magically make humans better. But you stop someone on the border or who might have a bit of shame already or who was on the path of becoming a fomor. You put their servants into disarray and mayhem and cause a civil war for another entity to take its place.<br /> <br /> That IS a victory for the Garou, and one they can profit from and use to lessen the grip of the Wyrm on the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T17:06:00-07:00","id":1536719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536178-could-killing-maeljin-incarna-actually-reduce-humanity-s-population?p=1536318#post1536318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the key here is that the Maeljin are not the causes of Evil. They are walking talking feedback loops of pettyness, abuse and horror. They feed of humans being horrible to each other, and they encourage people to be horrible in turn. This empowers them to do more crap in the world, whisper to susceptible people and create fomori and other direct or indirect servants.<br /> <br /> If you kill one of them, you do not remove the concepts of suffering from the world or magically stop humans from being mean assholes. You just stop that urge being proactive and lower its impact on the world. That doesn't mean you magically make humans better. But you stop someone on the border or who might have a bit of shame already or who was on the path of becoming a fomor. You put their servants into disarray and mayhem and cause a civil war for another entity to take its place.<br /> <br /> That IS a victory for the Garou, and one they can profit from and use to lessen the grip of the Wyrm on the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> My understanding is that everything, from trees, to cars, to ideas, are connected to spirits and have sprits. The example I saw in one book was that if you destroy or Calcify the spirit of a car, then the car will rapidly fall apart during the next week or two. The Maeljin are like a bridge between the physical world and Malfeas. These bridges allows the Wyrm to funnel the influence of Malfeas into the WoD. However, if the bridge is destroyed the Wyrm suddenly has a problem, because they are pieces of the Wyrm's very own soul. The Wyrm then is forced to regenerate the Maeljin and their duchies, and it does so by summoning Banes from Earth and absorbing the spirits that correspond to the specific Maeljin and their duchies that died and/or were destroyed.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for the Wyrm, a 1-1 conversion rate is more the domain of the Weaver than the Wyrm, and so the process of rebuilding the lost piece of the Wyrm's soul is a centuries long process that involves the Wyrm absorbing vast amounts of a specific family of Banes. With these spirits gone and destroyed, the concepts and actions they are attached to become weaker and less common. Wyrm elements disintegrate into harmless ones, and people turn away form self-destructive patterns of behaviors that harm others. The reasons why they turn away from those behaviors superficially seem obvious, but the Fera will notice that a change in patterns is occurring, and they will figure out what happened when they see it is a world wide phenomenon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T09:25:00-07:00","id":1536751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536178-could-killing-maeljin-incarna-actually-reduce-humanity-s-population?p=1536719#post1536719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> My understanding is that everything, from trees, to cars, to ideas, are connected to spirits and have sprits. The example I saw in one book was that if you destroy or Calcify the spirit of a car, then the car will rapidly fall apart during the next week or two. The Maeljin are like a bridge between the physical world and Malfeas. These bridges allows the Wyrm to funnel the influence of Malfeas into the WoD. However, if the bridge is destroyed the Wyrm suddenly has a problem, because they are pieces of the Wyrm's very own soul. The Wyrm then is forced to regenerate the Maeljin and their duchies, and it does so by summoning Banes from Earth and absorbing the spirits that correspond to the specific Maeljin and their duchies that died and/or were destroyed.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for the Wyrm, a 1-1 conversion rate is more the domain of the Weaver than the Wyrm, and so the process of rebuilding the lost piece of the Wyrm's soul is a centuries long process that involves the Wyrm absorbing vast amounts of a specific family of Banes. With these spirits gone and destroyed, the concepts and actions they are attached to become weaker and less common. Wyrm elements disintegrate into harmless ones, and people turn away form self-destructive patterns of behaviors that harm others. The reasons why they turn away from those behaviors superficially seem obvious, but the Fera will notice that a change in patterns is occurring, and they will figure out what happened when they see it is a world wide phenomenon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because the Wyrm is the champion of suffering doesn't mean dark emotions and urges don't exist without it, such concepts will exist in the High Umbra as long as there are entities capable of conducting them, dreaming them or imagining them. The Maeljin Incarna are embodiments of corruption itself, of Wyrm's desire to make everything suffer imbued into specific individuals that serve as its avatars and agents to propagate suffering. Getting rid of them is great and will lower the amount of suffering in the world. But it won't fix mankind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T11:02:00-07:00","id":1536756,"title":"","content":"Given the essays by Ethan Skemp in the 2nd edition player's guide, the Wyrm's lesser heads only feed off of all the terrible things that happen, because those terrible things still happen in real life. It's not trying to set up a magical root cause, because that would mean that you could just win through repeated applications of violence, which is as bad as the notion in Exalted 2nd edition that you can just deploy Immaculate monks to beat up truculent gods so that they don't cause diseases (according to the core of Ex2, which... deviated from the cause of disease in real life in ways that compromised the grit of the setting and usefulness of Medicine as a concept).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}